diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 64433b6..2b29441 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
   The default, `"replace"`, keeps the previous behaviour.
 
 ### Changed
+- Mode switches run one at a time: D-Bus calls, the default mode at startup and the cleanup on
+  SIGTERM share one lock, and D-Bus calls are no longer handled in parallel tasks.
 - Configuration is read once at startup instead of on every use.
 - Configuration is searched in `/run` instead of `/var/run`, as UAPI.6 specifies.
 - A missing configuration is no longer an error: defaults are used.
@@ -26,6 +28,13 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
   reported, and listed by `--print-config`.
 
 ### Fixed
+- `set_mode` returns an error when the new gadget cannot be enabled or its service cannot be
+  started, instead of reporting the requested mode. The same applies to leaving netboot mode
+  and to a failed switch to host role.
+- `aoa_ffs_mode` is refused before the current gadget is touched: its gadget was created but
+  never enabled.
+- SIGTERM and SIGINT are handled from the start: a stop or restart while the default mode is
+  being applied waits for it instead of killing usb-signaller halfway through.
 - One gadget that cannot be parsed no longer makes loading the UDC fail, and a gadget without
   a linked function no longer crashes usb-signaller. The bound gadget is found through the
   UDC's `function` attribute.
